{"entries":[{"caption":"Conditional relationships between nightly mean relative humidity and bat acoustic activity for (a) low-, (b) mid-, and (c) high-frequency echolocation groups. Lines show posterior median expected numbers of 5-min detection intervals per night, with inner and outer ribbons representing 50% and 89% credible intervals, respectively. Predictions were generated across the observed relative-humidity range and averaged over the observed distribution of sampled days of year, with each site weighted equally; temperature and lunar phase were held at their reference values. Y-axis scales differ among panels to emphasize response shape and uncertainty within each frequency group.","key":"fig-humidity","order":{"number":2,"section":[1,4,1,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Summary of the acoustic sampling design and environmental conditions represented in the analysis. Environmental ranges are based on the site-night observations retained for modeling.","key":"tbl-study-summary","order":{"number":1,"section":[1,1,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Conditional relationships between nightly mean temperature and bat acoustic activity for (a) low-frequency, (b) mid-frequency, and (c) high-frequency echolocation groups at eight sites in the northern Sierra Nevada, California. Predictions were generated across the observed temperature range and averaged over the observed distribution of sampled days of year, with each site weighted equally; relative humidity and lunar phase were held at their reference values. Lines show posterior medians and shaded ribbons show 50%, 80%, and 89% credible intervals (darkest to lightest). Y-axis scales differ among panels to emphasize differences in response shape among frequency groups.","key":"fig-temperature","order":{"number":3,"section":[1,4,2,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Conditional relationships between lunar phase and bat acoustic activity for (a) low-, (b) mid-, and (c) high-frequency echolocation groups. Lunar phase is represented from 0 (new moon) to 1 (full moon). Lines show posterior median expected numbers of 5-min detection intervals per night, with inner and outer ribbons representing 50% and 89% credible intervals, respectively. Predictions were generated across the observed lunar-phase range and averaged over the observed distribution of sampled days of year, with each site weighted equally; temperature and relative humidity were held at their reference values. Y-axis scales differ among panels to emphasize response shape and uncertainty within each frequency group.","key":"fig-lunar","order":{"number":4,"section":[1,4,3,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Posterior contrasts in expected nightly bat activity across environmental gradients for low-, mid-, and high-frequency echolocation groups. Temperature and relative-humidity contrasts compare predictions at the 10th and 90th percentiles of the observed covariate distributions; lunar contrasts compare new moon (0) with full moon (1). Differences and ratios are posterior medians with 89% credible intervals. P(Δ > 0) is the posterior probability that predicted activity at the upper endpoint exceeds predicted activity at the lower endpoint. Predictions are conditional on the remaining covariates in the full environmental model.","key":"tbl-environmental-contrasts","order":{"number":2,"section":[1,4,4,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Seasonal variation in community-level bat acoustic activity across eight sites in the northern Sierra Nevada, California, April–October 2015. (a) Total seasonal pattern from the day-of-year model, shown as the posterior distribution of the equal-site averaged expected number of 5-min intervals per night in which a bat call occurred. (b) Conditional seasonal pattern from the environmental model after accounting for nightly mean temperature, relative humidity, and lunar phase; the curve is likewise averaged equally across sites. (c) Site-specific seasonal phenology from the total seasonal model. Thin gray lines show posterior median trajectories for individual sites; the black line and shaded bands show the equal-site averaged seasonal trajectory. In panels a and b, and for the average in panel c, lines indicate posterior medians and shaded bands indicate 50%, 80%, and 89% credible intervals from darkest to lightest.","key":"fig-seasonality","order":{"number":1,"section":[1,3,0,0,0,0,0]}}],"headings":["results","sampling-and-acoustic-activity","model-adequacy-and-diagnostics","seasonal-activity","echolocation-frequency-groups","frequency-dependent-humidity-responses","temperature-responses-among-frequency-groups","lunar-phase-responses-among-frequency-groups","environmental-contrasts"]}